name><name><surname>Campuzano</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Molecular analysis of the <italic>asense</italic> gene, a member of the <italic>achaete-scute</italic> complex of <italic>Drosophila melanogaster</italic>, and its novel role in optic lobe development.</article-title><source>Embo J</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>3553</fpage><lpage>3562</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2510998</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001178-Jarman1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jarman</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Brand</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jan</surname><given-names>LY</given-names></name><name><surname>Jan</surname><given-names>YN</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>The regulation and function of the helix-loop-helix gene, asense, in Drosophila neural precursors.</article-title><source>Development</source><volume>119</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>29</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8565819</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001178-Nolo1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nolo</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Abbott</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bellen</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Senseless, a Zn finger transcription factor, is necessary and sufficient for sensory organ development in Drosophila.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>102</volume><fpage>349</fpage><lpage>362</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10975525</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001178-JafarNejad1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jafar-Nejad</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Acar</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nolo</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Lacin</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Pan</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Senseless acts as a binary switch during sensory organ precursor selection.</article-title><source>Genes Dev</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>2966</fpage><lpage>2978</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14665671</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001178-Lai1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lai</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Drosophila tufted is a gain-of-function allele of the proneural gene amos.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>163</volume><fpage>1413</fpage><lpage>1425</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12702685</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001178-Royet1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Royet</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Reichhart</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffmann</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Sensing and signaling during infection in Drosophila.</article-title><source>Curr Opin Immunol</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>11</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15653304</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001178-Moussian1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moussian</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Roth</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Dorsoventral axis formation in the Drosophila embryo&#x02013;shaping and transducing a morphogen gradient.</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>R887</fpage><lpage>899</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16271864</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001178-Lemaitre1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lemaitre</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicolas</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Michaut</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Reichhart</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffmann</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>The dorsoventral regulatory gene cassette spatzle/Toll/cactus controls the potent antifungal response in Drosophila adults.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>86</volume><fpage>973</fpage><lpage>983</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8808632</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001178-Sitcheran1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sitcheran</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Cogswell</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Baldwin</surname><given-names>AS</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>NF-kappaB mediates inhibition of mesenchymal cell differentiation through a posttranscriptional gene silencing mechanism.</article-title><source>Genes Dev</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>2368</fpage><lpage>2373</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14522944</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001178-Cantera1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cantera</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Roos</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Engstrom</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-ti